Hi,

With up2date, you will get new versions of whatever RPMs you already
have installed.

If you have the Kernel source installed from RPM (ie you selected that
when you installed RedHat), you will get the newer kernel source as well
as the binary from up2date. (But you need to either change your config
or run up2date -u -f to get the kernel files, they are not auto updated
by default).

